# 🔬 ResearchLens

[![Streamlit App](https://static.streamlit.io/badges/streamlit_badge_black_white.svg)](https://researchlens-eyx9aykauqodtg4c8xrymk.streamlit.app/)

**ResearchLens** is an interactive Python and Streamlit application built to help students and researchers explore research hypotheses, analyze topic momentum, and visualize academic vs. real-world interest trends.

🔗 **Live Visualization:** [researchlens.streamlit.app](https://researchlens-eyx9aykauqodtg4c8xrymk.streamlit.app/)

---

## ✨ Key Features

- **Hypothesis & Topic Validation:** Built-in input sanitization and gibberish-string detection to ensure meaningful research queries.
- **Academic Corpus Matching:** Searches and analyzes relevant academic literature to evaluate topic coverage and publication frequency over time.
- **Smart Google Trends Fallback:** Automatically integrates and displays Google Trends interest graphs whenever a query has limited or unmatched papers in the local corpus.
- **Interactive Streamlit UI:** Clean, responsive interface powered by Streamlit session state management for seamless multi-query exploration.
- **Time-Series Data Processing:** Uses modern `pandas` quarter-end (`QE`) resampling and time-series aggregation in `src/engine.py` for accurate trend plotting.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Language:** Python 3.x
- **Web Framework:** [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/)
- **Data Processing:** `pandas`
- **Trend & Visualization Engine:** Custom analytics engine (`src/engine.py`) + Google Trends integration

